+# Tasks: Pastebin Service
+
+**Input**: Design documents from `/specs/001-pastebin-service/`
+
+**Prerequisites**: [plan.md](./plan.md), [spec.md](./spec.md), [research.md](./research.md),
+[data-model.md](./data-model.md), [contracts/](./contracts/), [quickstart.md](./quickstart.md)
+
+**Tests**: Test tasks ARE included and are mandatory for this feature. Constitution Principle III
+("Every Requirement Is Testable") and SC-008 require every functional requirement FR-001…FR-044 to
+be named by at least one `pytest` test; the requirement→test map in
+[data-model.md](./data-model.md#requirement-to-test-map) fixes the module and test names, and the
+Development Workflow gate requires tests to be written before the implementation that satisfies
+them. Each test task below lists the exact test names from that map.
+
+**Organization**: Tasks are grouped by user story so each story can be implemented, tested, and
+demonstrated independently.
+
+## Format: `[ID] [P?] [Story] Description`
+
+- **[P]**: Can run in parallel (different files, no dependencies on incomplete tasks)
+- **[Story]**: Which user story the task belongs to (US1, US2, US3, US4)
+- Exact file paths are given in every description
+
+## Path Conventions
+
+Single Python package under `src/`, flat `tests/` beside it (plan.md → Structure Decision). All
+paths below are relative to the repository root.
+
+- Runtime: `src/pastebin/__init__.py`, `src/pastebin/__main__.py`, `src/pastebin/server.py`,
+  `src/pastebin/store.py`
+- Tests: `tests/conftest.py`, `tests/test_*.py`
+- Root files: `README.md`, `pytest.ini`, `requirements-dev.txt`
+
