+## Phase 3: User Story 1 - Publish a snippet and share a link to it (Priority: P1) 🎯 MVP
+
+**Goal**: A caller can publish UTF-8 text and read it back, as structured data with its metadata and
+as the raw bytes, with unguessable identifiers and a one-time delete token in the create response.
+Snippets published in this phase never expire (lifetimes arrive in US2).
+
+**Independent Test**: Start against an empty storage directory, `POST /pastes` with
+`{"content": "hello"}`, confirm `201` with `id`, `delete_token`, and `url: /pastes/<id>`; `GET` that
+url and confirm `id`, the exact text, a `created_at` ending in `Z`, and `"expires_at": null`; `GET`
+`/pastes/<id>/raw` and confirm the body is byte-for-byte the submitted text with
+`Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8`; `GET` an id never issued and confirm `404`.
+
