+## Phase 6: User Story 4 - Snippets outlive a restart of the service (Priority: P3)
+
+**Goal**: The nominated storage directory is the sole source of truth, so a new instance started
+against it serves, reads, and deletes every snippet an earlier instance published, with expiry
+moments unchanged and original delete tokens still valid.
+
+**Independent Test**: Start against a storage path that does not exist, confirm it is created and
+the service serves normally; publish several snippets with and without `expires_in`; stop the
+service; start a new instance against the same directory; confirm each snippet reads back with the
+same `id`, `content`, `created_at`, and `expires_at`, that a snippet whose expiry passed while the
+service was stopped `404`s, and that an original delete token still deletes.
+
+### Tests for User Story 4 ⚠️
+
+> **Write this first and confirm it FAILS (or passes only where the design already satisfies it)
+> before T040–T043**
+
+- [ ] T039 [P] [US4] Write `tests/test_persistence.py` covering FR-029…FR-031 with the names from data-model.md, using the subprocess fixture so the process boundary is real: `test_fr029_paste_readable_from_new_instance_on_same_dir`, `test_fr030_id_content_created_at_expires_at_token_survive_restart`, `test_fr031_deleted_paste_not_resurrected_by_restart` — plus coverage of a snippet whose expiry moment passed while the service was stopped (spec US4 scenario 5)
+
